// The roster the witness folds. A step whose target is not in this list is not covered, which is
// why targets are declared here rather than inline: a new call site that re-inlines a literal pair
// is outside the join.
//
// THIS LIST IS ITSELF A HAND-MAINTAINED PARALLEL ENUMERATION, and naming only the inline hole
// understated the denominator problem. A target escapes this roster TWO ways, needing different
// mechanisms:
//
//   1. a `gunbc run` step spelling a literal entry/function pair inline, never declared as a
//      target -- invisible to any enumeration of declarations, because the pair is not a
//      declaration. Only a check over the emitted steps can see it.
//   2. a twentieth `data ..._target: GunbcRunStepTarget` declared correctly and simply NOT ADDED
//      HERE. It looks correct at its declaration site and silently under-reports on anything
//      that folds this list.
//
// The second is the open-denominator class already named and priced: `std.primitives`
// `primitive_contract_roster_note` records the identical shape over *_contract rows, its silent
// under-reporting, and its dissolution — derive the roster by enumerating the declarations once
// declaration introspection lands.
//
// That dissolution condition is SATISFIED for this roster: `decl_facts` is a registered builtin
// callable from ordinary `.dag`, so the nineteen can be derived by enumerating every module-scope
// `data` of type `GunbcRunStepTarget` in this module instead of being retyped here — at no extra
// cost to any consumer that already walks decl_facts, turning a fold over "the rows someone
// remembered to list" into a fold over "the rows that exist". Until that lands, hole 2 is open and
// this list is diligence, not a denominator.
//
// Counted at authoring: 33 declarations, 33 entries. That equality is the thing nothing checks.
fn gunbc_run_step_targets() -> List<GunbcRunStepTarget> {
  [
    gunbc_ci_fleet_reach_probe_target,
